--- Task 5 hard-delete safety: measured, then decided ---

FINDING: users.id has 92 foreign-key columns pointing at it, across 69 distinct public tables. 89 are ON DELETE NO ACTION and 3 are ON DELETE CASCADE.
       NO ACTION examples: assistant_activities.approved_by, assistant_activities.proposed_by, assistant_activities.user_id, assistant_autonomy_prefs.user_id, assistant_conversations.user_id, audit_log.user_id
       They include audit_log.user_id, deals.created_by, documents.created_by,
       entities.created_by, member_investments.user_id and users.invited_by —
       i.e. the audit trail and the provenance of essentially every record.
       CASCADE: deal_interest.user_id, deal_votes.user_id, user_roles.user_id
       Those three make the case STRONGER, not weaker: if the NO ACTION
       constraints were ever relaxed to let a delete succeed, they would
       silently take the member's votes and expressions of interest with them.
DECISION: a hard delete is NOT safe and was NOT built. DELETE /admin/users/{id} is implemented as ANONYMIZATION — the row is kept so every FK still resolves, and the PII on it is destroyed: auth0_sub cleared (this is what severs the login), email/full_name replaced with sentinels, avatar/profile/manager/invite cleared, every user_roles and user_permission_sets grant revoked, account marked inactive. The response says so in its own body (hard_deleted=false, anonymized=true) so the caller is never told a deletion happened.
[PASS] T5: the hard-delete-safety finding is real and measured — 92 FK columns across 69 public tables: 89 NO ACTION (incl. audit_log.user_id) + 3 CASCADE
[PASS] T5: a REAL hard DELETE on a user with one dependent row actually raises — attempted DELETE FROM users -> ForeignKeyViolationError: Key (id)=(99000000-0000-0000-0000-0000f0110006) is still referenced from table "audit_log".; row still present after rollback (one audit_log row was enough — a real member has hundreds)
[PASS] T5: DELETE anonymizes and SAYS SO (hard_deleted=false, anonymized=true) — response body reports hard_deleted=False, anonymized=True
[PASS] T5: the row SURVIVES (so the dependent audit_log row still resolves) — users row retained — every one of the 92 FK references stays valid
[PASS] T5: the PII is genuinely gone and the login is severed — email 'usermgmtfinish_verify_delete_2a@example.com' -> 'deleted-99000000-0000-0000-0000-0000f0110006@deleted.invalid', full_name -> 'Deleted account', auth0_sub -> NULL, is_active -> False
[PASS] T5: the anonymized identity can no longer reclaim its old row — signing in again with the same sub creates a NEW, empty account (52f58127-d19e-4de6-a1f5-7d027a67406c) rather than resuming the old one
[PASS] T5: an anonymized account cannot be re-deleted or reactivated — second DELETE -> 409; reactivate -> 409 (reactivating would produce an active account nobody can sign into)

